import "pkg:/source/enums/PlaybackEndReport.bs"
import "pkg:/source/utils/misc.bs"

' What one end of a stream reports to the server: one report per stream, and only a stream that
' played has a position worth saving.
'
' Every end posts to the same stopped endpoint, and the stop does more than save the position:
' it stops the session's transcode and releases a Live TV live stream this session reported
' playing (one it never did is released by a close instead, see endClosesLiveStream). So a
' stream that never played still reports its end, marked `Failed`. Jellyfin then skips only the
' user-data write (its OnPlaybackStopped, 10.7.7 through 12.1), where an unmarked stop would save
' the position the player read before its first frame, usually 0, over the resume point (#969).
'
' @param {string} playerState - the Video state that ended the stream: stopped, finished or error
' @param {boolean} isPlayReported - this stream's `start` was reported
' @param {boolean} isEndReported - this stream's end was already reported
' @param {boolean} isForceFinished - forceFinishPlayback ended it: it sets `finished` itself, so
'   the `stopped` its stop raises is not the report
' @returns {string} a PlaybackEndReport
function classifyPlaybackEnd(playerState as string, isPlayReported as boolean, isEndReported as boolean, isForceFinished as boolean) as string
  if isEndReported then return PlaybackEndReport.NONE
  if playerState = "error" then return PlaybackEndReport.FAILED
  if isForceFinished
    if playerState = "finished" then return PlaybackEndReport.FINISHED
    return PlaybackEndReport.NONE
  end if
  if not isPlayReported then return PlaybackEndReport.FAILED
  if playerState = "finished" then return PlaybackEndReport.FINISHED
  return PlaybackEndReport.STOPPED
end function

' Whether this end releases the stream's Live TV live stream with a close by id rather than with
' its stop. Exactly one of the two must release it: each release drops one consumer, and a
' second one, on a stream the server shares between viewers, ends another viewer's stream.
'
' A live stream that never reported its start (a direct play that failed over to transcode, a
' restart that ended at once, an error before the first frame) cannot rely on its stop, because
' what the server does with that stop depends on its version and on who else is watching:
' 10.7–10.10 always release, 10.11 never does (it releases only a session linked by a `start` or
' progress report, jellyfin#13220), and 12.x does only while no other session is linked
' (jellyfin#17178). So the close releases it, and the stop does not name the stream
' (liveStreamReportFields), which leaves it alone on every version. jellyfin-kodi ends every
' live stream the same way.
'
' A stream that did report its start is released by its stop, as the server expects, and never
' closed here as well.
'
' @param {string} report - the PlaybackEndReport this end sends (classifyPlaybackEnd)
' @param {boolean} isPlayReported - this stream's `start` was reported
' @param {dynamic} liveStreamId - the stream's LiveStreamId; invalid or empty when it has none
' @returns {boolean}
function endClosesLiveStream(report as string, isPlayReported as boolean, liveStreamId as dynamic) as boolean
  if report = PlaybackEndReport.NONE then return false
  if isPlayReported then return false
  return isValidAndNotEmpty(liveStreamId)
end function

' The Live TV fields a playback report carries. Every report names the media source, and every
' report names the live stream except the end of one that a close releases (endClosesLiveStream):
' a stop naming it would release it a second time on the servers that act on it.
'
' @param {object} transcodeParams - the stream's MediaSourceId and LiveStreamId
' @param {boolean} closesLiveStream - this report is an end whose live stream a close releases
' @returns {object} the fields to append to the report
function liveStreamReportFields(transcodeParams as object, closesLiveStream as boolean) as object
  fields = { "MediaSourceId": transcodeParams.MediaSourceId }
  ' Bracketed, because a dot assignment would send the key lower-cased (`livestreamid`).
  if not closesLiveStream then fields["LiveStreamId"] = transcodeParams.LiveStreamId
  return fields
end function

' The live stream a video load opened and then failed to hand over, or "" when it left none.
'
' LoadVideoContentTask asks PlaybackInfo to open a live stream, then can still fail building the
' stream's URL (no transcoding URL from the server, a localhost path it cannot rebuild, no server
' URL). The player then shows the error without ever holding the stream, so no end report, and no
' endClosesLiveStream, can reach it: the load has to close it itself. A load that succeeded hands
' the stream to the player, which closes it.
'
' @param {object} video - the load's own result AA (its `content` is invalid when it failed)
' @returns {string} the LiveStreamId to close, or ""
function liveStreamLeftByFailedLoad(video as object) as string
  if isValid(video.content) then return ""
  if not isValid(video.transcodeParams) then return ""
  liveStreamId = video.transcodeParams.LiveStreamId
  if not isValidAndNotEmpty(liveStreamId) then return ""
  return liveStreamId
end function
